## What you can do
With this project, you can give a llm a hand to the outside world. no complex protocols and standards, just simple thing a model actually needs to use the hand

## Chat with a local Llama server

Start a Llama server with its OpenAI-compatible API listening on port 8080, then run `npm start` or `node chat.js`. `chat.js` handles the terminal conversation, while `llama.js` handles API requests and streams replies as they are generated. When the model calls a tool, the chat class runs it, sends the result back to the model, and continues until the model responds without another tool call. Conversation history is kept until you enter `/exit` or `/quit`.

## Tool-calling classes

`chat.js` is the entry point and starts `CompatibilityChat` directly. Its compatibility-specific prompt and response parsing live in that class; shared conversation and tool-execution behavior lives in the parent `Chat` class.

`CompatibilityChat` includes tool definitions and calling instructions in the system prompt, parses tool calls from the response text, and sends results as `user` messages. `ToolSupportingModelChat` sends tool definitions to llama.cpp's built-in tool-calling API, does not add tool instructions to the system prompt, and sends tool results as `tool` messages. In either mode, `load_image` also sends a separate `user` message containing the image. To switch the entry point to `ToolSupportingModelChat`, change the class instantiated at the bottom of `chat.js`.

The `load_image` tool reads PNG, JPEG, GIF, or WebP files from disk. In `CompatibilityChat`, the image is sent in a separate user message using the OpenAI-compatible `image_url` content format; the connected model must support vision. Ollama's native chat API also attaches images to user messages (using its `images` field), rather than returning them as tool results.

Both classes are exported from `chat.js`. Importing `chat.js` starts the configured chat entry point.

The default endpoint is `http://localhost:8080/v1/chat/completions`. Set `LLAMA_URL` to override it.